# Line-ending normalization.
#
# Git stores text with LF and checks it out with LF on every platform, so a
# clone on Windows gets the same bytes as one on macOS or Linux.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. That breaks any script executed inside a Linux
# container: docker/init-db/01-init.sh is marked executable, so Postgres execs
# it, and the shebang line becomes "#!/bin/bash\r" — an interpreter that does
# not exist. Initialization aborts, the interakt databases are never created,
# and the healthcheck (pg_isready -d interakt) leaves the container unhealthy.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts run by Linux containers are always LF, regardless of detection.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts are always CRLF, should any be added.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files — never inspected or converted.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
